What is in each package
-----------------------

  - llama.cpp and ggml, built as static libraries: llama, llama-common,
    ggml-base, ggml-cpu and one GPU backend (ggml-cuda in the CUDA packages,
    ggml-vulkan in the Vulkan packages). Inside ggml, sgemm.cpp (tinyBLAS)
    and the YaRN RoPE code (in ggml-cpu and ggml-cuda) carry their own
    notices, reproduced below. The Vulkan backend also embeds ggml's compute
    shaders, compiled to SPIR-V at build time from ggml's own sources and
    covered by the llama.cpp / ggml license.
  - From llama.cpp's vendor/ directory: cpp-httplib (HTTP server and the
    HTTPS client for Hugging Face downloads) and nlohmann/json. Nothing else
    from that directory ends up in the executable: no miniaudio, stb,
    sheredom/subprocess.h or the hash libraries (xxhash, sha1, sha256), and
    no llguidance.
  - LibreSSL 4.4.0, downloaded from the official release by llama.cpp's
    build and linked statically (libssl and libcrypto), used only for the
    HTTPS connections of the model downloads.
  - zlib, linked statically: from Ubuntu 22.04 (zlib1g-dev) in the Linux
    packages and from vcpkg in the Windows packages.
  - Vulkan packages only: Vulkan-Headers (vulkan.h, vulkan_core.h,
    vulkan.hpp) and SPIRV-Headers (spirv.hpp), from the LunarG Vulkan SDK.
    They are header-only: their inline code and constants are compiled into
    ggml-vulkan.
  - The web interface, embedded in the executable (gzipped): the JavaScript
    bundle contains the Svelte 5 client runtime and three.js (core plus the
    OrbitControls, EffectComposer, RenderPass, UnrealBloomPass and
    OutputPass add-ons, which are part of the three package). The bundle
    does not contain Svelte's compiler or any of its other dependencies
    (clsx, devalue and esm-env are absent or reduced to build-time
    constants). The fonts are WOFF2 files: JetBrains Mono (Regular, Bold)
    and Inter (latin subset, weights 400, 500 and 600).
  - Linux packages: libgomp.so.1 (GNU OpenMP runtime, used by ggml's CPU
    threads), copied unmodified from Ubuntu 22.04. The executable is built
    with GCC 11.4.0, so it also contains code from GCC's headers and startup
    objects, covered by the same GCC Runtime Library Exception.
  - CUDA packages: NVIDIA's CUDA runtime and cuBLAS libraries, unmodified
    (libcudart.so.12, libcublas.so.12, libcublasLt.so.12 on Linux;
    cudart64_12.dll, cublas64_12.dll, cublasLt64_12.dll on Windows). The
    GPU kernels are compiled with the CUDA Toolkit and include template code
    from its headers (CUB, Thrust and libcu++, also published by NVIDIA as
    CCCL: https://github.com/NVIDIA/cccl).
  - Windows packages: the Microsoft Visual C++ runtime and OpenMP runtime
    DLLs, unmodified (msvcp140.dll, vcruntime140.dll, vcruntime140_1.dll,
    vcomp140.dll).

Not distributed, provided by the user's system: on Linux, glibc,
libstdc++.so.6 and libgcc_s.so.1 (linked dynamically); on Windows, the
Universal C Runtime (part of Windows); and the GPU driver's libraries
(libcuda.so.1 / nvcuda.dll, libvulkan.so.1 / vulkan-1.dll). Build tools
(CMake, Ninja, the compilers, glslc, Vite, TypeScript and the other web
development dependencies) are used only to build inside-llm and are not part
of the packages.


